# Precedence

Project rules override these; repository documentation (`/docs`, `README.md`, ADRs) overrides
both. Prefer the simplest solution; project conventions beat skill defaults; say so plainly when
no skill applies rather than inventing a process.

Machine-local specifics — Jira project keys, boards, documentation repositories, cluster names —
live in `~/.cursor/local/`, unversioned (symlinked to `~/.claude/local/`). Read the file a
command or skill names; if it is missing, ask rather than guess.

Commands, agents, and skills each own one layer and never restate another's. Each command carries
its own dispatch contract; `~/.claude/skills/ai-config/SKILL.md` owns the rest, and its
`references/agent-architecture.md` owns the agent model.
